---
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro"
import Fact from "../../components/Fact.astro"
import { teamTrial } from "../../site"

const sections: [string, string][] = [
  ["short", "In short"],
  ["no-refunds", "No refunds"],
  ["cancel", "Cancelling"],
  ["trial", "The Team trial"],
  ["consent", "Starting at once"],
  ["statutory", "Rights the law gives you"],
  ["mistakes", "Billing mistakes"],
  ["contact", "Questions and complaints"],
]
---

<Legal slug="refunds" description="Paperboat payments are not refunded. Cancelling stops the next renewal. How this works with consumer law." {sections}>
  <p slot="intro">
    Every feature is free for personal use, so you can try Paperboat fully before you pay. Because of that, payments are final. This page says
    exactly what that means and where the law gives you more.
  </p>

  <section id="short">
    <h2>In short</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <ul>
        <li>Payments for plans, seats and extra bandwidth are not refunded, in full or in part.</li>
        <li>You can cancel at any time. Cancelling stops the next renewal; your plan keeps working until the end of the period you paid for.</li>
        <li>There are no prorated refunds for cancelling, downgrading, removing seats or unused bandwidth.</li>
        <li>The Team trial costs nothing if you cancel before it ends.</li>
        <li>If we charge you by mistake, we put it right.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="no-refunds">
    <h2>No refunds</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        When you pay for a plan, extra seats or extra bandwidth, the service starts at once and you can use all of it straight away. We do not
        refund those payments, in full or in part, including when:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>you cancel, or stop using Paperboat, before the end of a period;</li>
        <li>you move to a cheaper plan or from yearly to monthly;</li>
        <li>you remove seats from a team (removed seats stay paid until the next billing date);</li>
        <li>extra bandwidth you bought is not used before it ends;</li>
        <li>you forgot to cancel before a renewal;</li>
        <li>we suspend or close your account because it broke the <a href="/legal/terms/">Terms</a> or the <a href="/legal/acceptable-use/">Acceptable Use Policy</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The one exception is our own decision: if we close your account without a breach on your part, or stop offering the hosted service,
        we refund the unused part of any period you paid for in advance (<a href="/legal/terms/#suspension">Terms, section 8</a>).
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="cancel">
    <h2>Cancelling</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Paid plans renew automatically, monthly or yearly, until you cancel. Cancel in the console under <strong>Billing</strong>, at any time,
        in a few clicks; you do not need to contact us. After you cancel, your plan keeps working until the end of the current period and is
        not charged again. When it ends, the workspace moves to the Free plan's limits. Your machines and data stay unless you delete them.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can undo a cancellation before the period ends with <strong>Keep plan</strong>. If a renewal payment fails, we tell you and retry;
        the plan ends if it is still unpaid after the grace period shown on the <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="trial">
    <h2>The Team trial</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>{teamTrial} Once the first charge is taken, it is covered by this policy like any other payment.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="consent">
    <h2>Starting at once</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Before every purchase, Checkout asks you to tick a box that says:
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        <p>
          “Start the service now. I agree to the Terms of Service and the Refund Policy: the plan renews automatically until I cancel,
          cancelling stops the next renewal, and payments are not refunded. I ask for the service to start during the 14-day withdrawal
          period and understand that if I withdraw, I pay for the service up to that point.”
        </p>
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        You cannot buy without ticking it. We confirm the purchase, and this consent, in the receipt we email you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="statutory">
    <h2>Rights the law gives you</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Nothing on this page takes away a right that the law of your country gives you and that cannot be given up by agreement. In
        particular:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Consumers in the European Union, the EEA and the United Kingdom</strong> have 14 days to withdraw from an online purchase.
          At Checkout you ask us to start the service during that time. If you withdraw, tell us within the 14 days by email to <Fact name="legalEmail" /> with a clear statement that you
          withdraw. We then refund what you paid for that period, minus an amount in proportion to the service you received up to the time you
          told us, within 14 days, to the same payment method.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Consumers in India</strong> keep their rights under the Consumer Protection Act, 2019, including where a service was not
          provided as described. Complaints go to our grievance officer (below).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Everyone</strong> keeps any right to a remedy for a service that was not provided at all, or not as described, and any right
          the law of their country does not allow a contract to exclude.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These rights apply to consumers. A purchase made wholly or mainly for business purposes is not a consumer purchase, and then payments
        are final; the plan's name alone does not decide this.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="mistakes">
    <h2>Billing mistakes</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        If you were charged twice, charged after a cancellation took effect, or charged an amount different from the price shown at Checkout,
        tell us within 60 days of the charge. We check it and return the wrong amount to the same payment method. This is correcting our
        mistake, not a refund.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please contact us before you dispute a charge with your bank. A chargeback on a correct charge may lead us to suspend the workspace
        until it is settled.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <h2>Questions and complaints</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Write to <Fact name="legalEmail" />. Grievance officer (India Consumer Protection (E-Commerce) Rules, 2020): <Fact name="grievanceOfficer" />,
        at the same address. We acknowledge a complaint within 48 hours and answer it within one month.
      </p>
      <p>Paperboat, operated by <Fact name="operators" />. Postal address: <Fact name="address" />.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Legal>
